{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "20034",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.21,
      "end_seconds": 5.51,
      "duration_seconds": 4.3,
      "text": "Hello? Doctor? I was told to come in."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 6.65,
      "end_seconds": 10.45,
      "duration_seconds": 3.8,
      "text": "Yes, have a seat. Tell me what's going on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 11.62,
      "end_seconds": 20.83,
      "duration_seconds": 9.21,
      "text": "Mainly my heart racing. There's a couple of other things, uh, but that's the main one."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 21.51,
      "end_seconds": 24.64,
      "duration_seconds": 3.13,
      "text": "Is there any regular medication you use?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 25.46,
      "end_seconds": 28.25,
      "duration_seconds": 2.79,
      "text": "Nothing regular, you know, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 37.19,
      "end_seconds": 39.28,
      "duration_seconds": 2.09,
      "text": "Did it come on recently?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 42.78,
      "end_seconds": 49.13,
      "duration_seconds": 6.35,
      "text": "around about three months... no wait, it's more like about a month"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 49.69,
      "end_seconds": 58.77,
      "duration_seconds": 9.08,
      "text": "Tell me a bit more about it: how bad it gets, how often, and whether anything makes it better or worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 60.35,
      "end_seconds": 73.06,
      "duration_seconds": 12.71,
      "text": "It happens all the time. I'd say severe. I'm not great at remembering details, so bear with me. I'm hoping you can tell me something definite."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 73.77,
      "end_seconds": 77.75,
      "duration_seconds": 3.98,
      "text": "Has there been a trembling in your hands too?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 78.35,
      "end_seconds": 80.09,
      "duration_seconds": 1.74,
      "text": "yeah, that too"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 81.39,
      "end_seconds": 84.33,
      "duration_seconds": 2.94,
      "text": "any neck swelling, eye pain or fainting?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 85.41,
      "end_seconds": 90.51,
      "duration_seconds": 5.1,
      "text": "Oh, you know, no, none of those at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 94.21,
      "end_seconds": 98.04,
      "duration_seconds": 3.83,
      "text": "What about your tummy and bowels, anything unusual there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 98.83,
      "end_seconds": 102.83,
      "duration_seconds": 4.0,
      "text": "bowels are regular, you know, nothing odd"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 104.15,
      "end_seconds": 108.21,
      "duration_seconds": 4.06,
      "text": "Any medical conditions, anything you've been treated for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 110.25,
      "end_seconds": 113.06,
      "duration_seconds": 2.81,
      "text": "no, I've always been fairly healthy"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 132.02,
      "end_seconds": 136.5,
      "duration_seconds": 4.48,
      "text": "Has anything ever caused you a reaction? I mean any allergies."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 138.03,
      "end_seconds": 140.87,
      "duration_seconds": 2.84,
      "text": "I've never had an allergy."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 142.05,
      "end_seconds": 144.6,
      "duration_seconds": 2.55,
      "text": "Have you had any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 145.39,
      "end_seconds": 149.58,
      "duration_seconds": 4.19,
      "text": "I mean, no, I've never been operated on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 162.58,
      "end_seconds": 166.52,
      "duration_seconds": 3.94,
      "text": "let's talk a little about your daily life and habits"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 168.15,
      "end_seconds": 184.71,
      "duration_seconds": 16.56,
      "text": "I smoke roughly a pack every two days. I drink a lot of tea and snack through the day. My husband and I live above the shop. Not much, I mostly stay in these days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 186.3,
      "end_seconds": 188.86,
      "duration_seconds": 2.56,
      "text": "Let's start with the basic checks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 202.56,
      "end_seconds": 205.27,
      "duration_seconds": 2.71,
      "text": "That's it, just a little longer..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 224.82,
      "end_seconds": 236.09,
      "duration_seconds": 11.27,
      "text": "Okay: saturation 96 percent, temperature is 36.8 degrees, weight 55 kilos, height 177 centimetres, BP is 126 over 76, pulse is 123 beats a minute."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 238.7,
      "end_seconds": 242.37,
      "duration_seconds": 3.67,
      "text": "Now I'm going to do a short physical check."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 244.08,
      "end_seconds": 246.25,
      "duration_seconds": 2.17,
      "text": "hold that for a second"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 254.63,
      "end_seconds": 259.5,
      "duration_seconds": 4.87,
      "text": "there is a smooth, small swelling at the front of the neck"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 260.86,
      "end_seconds": 263.09,
      "duration_seconds": 2.23,
      "text": "I'm just checking this side."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 271.58,
      "end_seconds": 278.59,
      "duration_seconds": 7.01,
      "text": "There is a fine tremor of the outstretched hands and the pulse is fast and regular."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 297.38,
      "end_seconds": 298.37,
      "duration_seconds": 0.99,
      "text": "Sure thing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 303.98,
      "end_seconds": 339.41,
      "duration_seconds": 35.43,
      "text": "That's the examination finished. Taking everything into account, it fits best with an overactive thyroid. I'm sending you for an ECG because of palpitations. I'm going to put you on propranolol, 20 milligrams, twice a day, until review. You take it by mouth. It's for racing heart and tremor. Try to avoid caffeine while we sort this out. I'm not ordering thyroid blood tests today. If things carry on next month, we'll consider it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 341.11,
      "end_seconds": 358.34,
      "duration_seconds": 17.23,
      "text": "The thing that would worry me is if the symptoms get worse. If that happens, go to emergency. Let's plan a check after the thyroid results. Right, is there anything you'd like me to go over again?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 359.96,
      "end_seconds": 363.36,
      "duration_seconds": 3.4,
      "text": "okay, that makes sense thanks for explaining"
    }
  ]
}